During pv-controller volume sync, if the corresponding claim key is simply re-added to the queue, significant time may be consumed when the queue is large and contains many PVCs unable to locate resources (as all PVs will be traversed). This can lead to prolonged delays in batch scheduling scenarios. The proposed modification greatly improves speed by directly binding the PV and PVC:

Code changes as follows:
```
// In both cases, the volume is Bound and the claim is Pending.
			// direct bind pv & pvc to improve bind speed
			newClaim, err := ctrl.kubeClient.CoreV1().PersistentVolumeClaims(claim.Namespace).Get(ctx, claim.Name, metav1.GetOptions{})
			if err != nil {
				klog.Errorf("Get Claim %s/%s error %v", claim.Namespace, claim.Name)
				return err
			}

			if err := ctrl.bind(ctx, volume, newClaim); err != nil {
				return err
			}
```

